A.BI=s(["taulnama is a register you keep. The printed sheet is your own record, prepared from what you typed. It is not a government document and it is not evidence of verification \u2014 your stamped certificate is.","This sheet records WHEN an instrument was stamped and when that period ends. It says nothing about whether the instrument weighs correctly. It is not a calibration or an accuracy check, and there is no compliance verdict on it anywhere.","If the instrument has been repaired, or dismantled and re-installed, since it was last stamped, Rule 27(3)\u2013(4) requires re-verification before it is put back into use \u2014 whatever days-left this sheet shows. taulnama cannot know that happened, so it cannot apply it for you.","Which clause an instrument falls in is a READING, not a ruling. Clause (a) names beam scales, counter machines and weights at twenty-four months; an electronic or spring balance is not named there, so taulnama puts it in the residual clause (c) at twelve. If your inspector treats your electronic counter scale as a counter machine, the period is 24 \u2014 change it on the row, and this sheet will print your number with the default beside it.","The three periods come from Rule 27(2) of the Legal Metrology (General) Rules, 2011, quoted verbatim with the source link and the date we read it. Rules change and states amend them. Confirm with your Legal Metrology office before relying on a date.","The next-due date is the same calendar day, N months after the stamp date, clamped to the end of a short month (a 29 Feb stamp becomes 28 Feb), and the sheet says so on any row where the clamp applied.","DEPARTMENTS RECKON BY QUARTER, NOT BY DAY. The stamp records the year and the QUARTER of verification \u2014 (A) Jan\u2013Mar, (B) Apr\u2013Jun, (C) Jul\u2013Sep, (D) Oct\u2013Dec \u2014 and carries no day at all; re-verification is commonly treated as falling due within the corresponding quarter, and penalty fees are charged per quarter or part of one. So a scale stamped in July is generally treated as due through the whole July\u2013September quarter. Every days figure here is the day-exact arithmetic, not your department's calendar: where the date has passed but its quarter has not, a row says PAST THE DATE and names that quarter, never OVERDUE. Confirm the date on your certificate with your Legal Metrology office.","Stamping fees are UNCITED. They are notified state by state and taulnama ships none. Every fee on this sheet is one you typed off your own receipt. A fee split across instruments is largest-remainder to the paisa: the parts always sum exactly to the receipt total, but one instrument may differ by a paisa from a naive share.","An empty register shows nothing. It does not mean you are up to date \u2014 it means nothing has been entered yet.","Local-first: your register is a SQLite file on your machine and the app runs on localhost. No accounts, no sync, no encryption, no cloud. Nothing you type is uploaded, and the demo page stores nothing. The one network path in the Flutter engine is its font fallback: left unset, a character missing from the bundled fonts makes the engine fetch a substitute from fonts.gstatic.com. taulnama pins that base URL to its own assets folder, so the request cannot leave this page \u2014 a genuinely missing glyph is simply not drawn. The printed sheets go further and assert, in the embedded font, that every character they lay out has a glyph."],t.s)
